###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120094
:MILD_120094 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
             rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                           owl:unionOf ( <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016>
                                         :MILD_120005
                                       )
                         ] ;
             rdfs:range <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040> ;
             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "b has material basis c =Def b is a disposition or a tendency & c is a material entity & there is some d bearer of b & there is some time t such that c is a continuant part of d at t & d has b because c is a continuant part of d at t"@en ;
             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "DESIGN RATIONALE - MILD-owned widening of BFO_0000218 'has material basis'. BFO declares that property with rdfs:domain BFO_0000016 disposition, because BFO has no tendency category. MILD does (MILD_120005), and MILD_120005 states that a tendency, like a disposition, supervenes on the physical makeup of its bearer - so tendencies have material bases too. The domain here is therefore the union of disposition and tendency; range, definition and scope note are otherwise taken unchanged from BFO_0000218, with the definiens widened only by the disjunction. This property is deliberately NOT declared rdfs:subPropertyOf BFO_0000218: a subproperty inherits its parent's domain, which would reimpose disposition and make every tendency-based class unsatisfiable. It is also not asserted by patching BFO itself, because rdfs:domain axioms conjoin rather than union - adding a second domain narrows to the intersection - and owl:imports is monotonic, so BFO's original axiom cannot be retracted. The relation to the BFO property is recorded with skos:relatedMatch."@en ;
             rdfs:label "has a material basis"@en ;
             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#relatedMatch> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000218> ;
             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Users that require more sophisticated representations of time are encouraged to import a temporal extension of BFO-Core provided by the BFO development team. See documentation for guidance: <https://github.com/BFO-ontology/BFO-2020/tree/master/src/owl/profiles/temporal%20extensions>"@en .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120101
:MILD_120101 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
             rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053> ;
             rdfs:domain <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004> ;
             rdfs:range :MILD_120005 ;
             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "b has tendency t =Def t is a tendency (MILD_120005) & t inheres in b"@en ;
             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "DESIGN RATIONALE (2026-10-03) - the bearer relation for MILD's tendency category, parallel to RO_0000091 'has disposition'. MILD makes disposition, role and tendency pairwise disjoint, while RO_0000091 has the range BFO_0000016 disposition; WONT bore 'wound infecting tendency' by RO_0000091 (Staphylococcus aureus, Escherichia coli, WONT_120019), which made those classes and MRSA infection unsatisfiable under the import closure (ELK and HermiT). Declared a subproperty of RO_0000053 'has characteristic', whose range specifically dependent continuant a tendency satisfies, and not of RO_0000091, whose range would reimpose disposition."@en ;
             rdfs:label "has tendency"@en .


